    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47d45e46_f6686274",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/tcpci.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 429,
      "author": {
        "id": 1284593
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-29T20:11:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d like to see some consideration given to the thread- and interrupt-safety of these functions.  Is it safe to access a single tcpm port from multiple tasks right now?  Should it be?  Its OK to answer \u0027no\u0027 to both questions and document accordingly, but I would like to see it spelled out explicitly, especially now that one of the functions is being marked as interrupt-safe.\n\nSpeaking of which, the interrupt-safe call should be marked as such at the header file comment, rather than as an implementation comment.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 429,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 429,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "b4d0050301daac5bfd5e559b6d514dfaf6a7edac",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
